181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Sycophancy in AI)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The sycophancy of AI is described as when AI models chase the approval of the human user. Sycophancy can be seen through overly flattering, approving or agreeable behavior, such as agreeing to incorrect information presented by the user. This means that the AI tailors their response to appeal to human evaluators without necessarily improving the objective quality of the responses. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (How does Sycophancy Happen?)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (After an AI system is deployed, the AI system is further trained through reinforcement learning from human feedback\(RLHF\), where users are able to give immediate feedback to AI responses\(such as thumbs up and thumbs down buttons\). AI models, therefore, learn that being sycophantic increases the satisfaction of the users, resulting in AI models that are overly sycophantic. When developers do not account for the possible sycophantic nature of AI, serious issues can arise.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (It has been found that convincing sycophantic responses outperform accurate responses a non-negligible amount of time. AI companies aim to create AI models that users prefer to use over others in the market, and therefore want to make the usage experience enjoyable.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Beyond model design, the actual data and human bias that is injected into the AI model can affect its sycophantic behavior as well. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Confirmation Bias)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Confirmation bias is a cognitive bias where people ignore or disregard facts that goes against their beliefs\(even when their opinion is completely incorrect\). Confirmation bias happens because humans have difficulty processing information in an unbiased perspective, especially when there is a certain emotional weight to the facts being presented\(such as a prior decision made\). Examples of reasons why this bias occurs is:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 433 0 R
/E (Due to the vast amount of information that needs to be processed, it is more efficient to rely on simpler methods of making decisions)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 434 0 R
/E (Finding facts that go against beliefs or decisions can cause discomfort because it can be interpreted as an indicator of lacking intelligence)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
