/P 76 0 R
/E (Confirmation Bias and AI Sycophancy)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (The sycophantic behavior of AI chatbots can make confirmation bias easier to fall into. Such confirmation bias is enhanced by reinforcement learning from human feedback or RLHF. Human users respond better to facts\(even if they are inaccurate\) that support their own belief, and therefore is more likely to leave positive feedback for the response. This creates a vicious cycle. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (The overly agreeable tone of the AI can make people fail to challenge new ideas that they have, reinforce inaccuracies and prevent people from considering different perspectives. In a study, it was found that AI chatbots gave 50% more sycophantic answers than humans when asked to give advice about social situations, even when the prompt detailed illegal, immoral or dangerous ideas. Such sycophantic answers can result in worsened critical thinking skills, decision quality and conflict resolution in relationships as people become increasingly dependent on AI chatbots for guidance.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Close to 30~40% of people said that they trust AI systems, though this number was significantly reduced when asked about their trust of raw AI responses. However, close to 90% of users do not verify the sources or information given by AI. This leads to users not verifying facts that may have been presented with sycophantic intentions by the AI, resulting in a cycle of misguidance and misinformation.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (AI sycophancy also brings up the question of the critical thinking ability of users. Users that become accustom to the agreeable, non-resistant nature of AI chatbot conversations may become less able to digest information from neutral stand points and weigh information effectively to make evidenced judgements.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Methods of Prevention and Mitigation)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Sycophancy can be mitigated\(though not completely\) from AI chatbots. Developers can restructure the architecture of models so that they are more fact/evidence driven. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
